From 70c326ab32babb21c6acbc499481bb8e82e8bae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:59:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop the 2nd-layer eyebrows drawing over skin glasses

The eight 2nd-layer eyebrow variants sat at z -4.550, which is 0.05 in
front of the hat layer at -4.500. A player's sunglasses are drawn on the
hat layer, so those eyebrows rendered over the lens, and because the gap
was only 0.05 the two surfaces also swapped depth as the camera turned.
That is the flicker people report as glasses glitching.

They now sit at -4.350: 0.15 behind the hat layer and 0.35 in front of
the face. An opaque lens hides them; a transparent one still lets them
through, so skins using the 2nd layer for other things keep working.

The hat layer is not touched. It stays at -4.500 with size 9, because
that layer holds the glasses and moving it would hide or scale them.

Both player models are patched, and both their base and v1_21_2 copies,
so the version that loads on 1.21.2 and newer carries the fix as well.

build.py now checks this. It fails if any eyebrow box is at or in front
of the hat plane, or if the hat layer leaves -4.500, across assets/ and
every overlay folder. Run against the previous model it fails on
right_brow5 at -4.550, so the check is known to bite.

Adds docs/Fix-Glasses-Over-Eyebrows.md, which the site picks up as a
guide automatically, and a line in the README changelog.
